BT /F2 15 Tf 72 701.0 Td (Latent Diffusion Model to Remove Motion Artifacts in Neonatal MRI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 676.8 Td (Quanhao Sun, Yaqiong Chai, Steven Li, Duan Xu, Michael Khoo, Hosung Kim) Tj ET
BT /F1 9 Tf 72 660.7 Td (University of Southern California, Los Angeles, CA; University of California San Francisco, San Francisco, CA) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.5 Tf 72 642.0 Td (Biomedical Engineering Society \(BMES\) Annual Meeting, 2025. Track: Biomedical Imaging and Instrumentation - Deep) Tj ET
BT /F3 9.5 Tf 72 628.2 Td (Learning and Artificial Intelligence in Biomedical Imaging and Instrumentation.) Tj ET
0.72 w 0.72 0.72 0.72 RG 72 620.2 m 540 620.2 l S
BT /F2 11 Tf 72 590.2 Td (Introduction) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 572.0 Td (Neonatal brain MRI is a critical imaging method for assessing early brain development and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 556.8 Td (neurodevelopmental abnormalities and guiding clinical interventions. However, acquiring high-quality images) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 541.5 Td (in neonates is challenging because infants cannot remain still during image acquisition, and sedation is often) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 526.3 Td (not feasible. Their scans are thus frequently affected by motion artifacts. Neurodevelopmental features such as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 511.1 Td (growing brains, incomplete cortical folding, ongoing myelination, and indistinct gray/white matter boundaries) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 495.9 Td (make the appearance of neonatal brains different from adult brains. Motion artifacts can easily obscure these) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 480.6 Td (important features and significantly impact downstream analyses.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 458.4 Td (Conventional motion correction approaches, including k-space interpolation, rigid-body registration, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 443.2 Td (convolutional neural network \(CNN\)-based post-processing, often perform poorly on neonatal data. Most) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 428.0 Td (approaches utilize simulated motions that are often too simplified or rely on paired data where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 412.7 Td (motion-corrupted and clean images are available, which are difficult to obtain in pediatric imaging. These) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 397.5 Td (methods often lack robust modelling of various patterns of motion common in neonates.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 375.3 Td (Recently, generative diffusion models have emerged as a powerful alternative. They offer a probabilistic) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 360.1 Td (framework capable of learning data-driven priors and reconstructing clean images from noisy observations. In) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 344.8 Td (this study, we extend our previously developed Motion Adaptive Diffusion Model \(MADM\) to neonatal brain) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 329.6 Td (MRI. Trained on high-quality, artifact-free infant images, MADM learns the structural patterns of neonatal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 314.4 Td (anatomy and predicts clean images from motion-corrupted images without needing paired supervision. In this) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 299.2 Td (study, we apply MADM to a very challenging task of head-motion correction on neonatal brain MRI and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 283.9 Td (compare its performance with a CNN approach.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 72 255.0 Td (Materials and Methods) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 236.8 Td (This study utilized a neonatal brain MRI dataset comprising 325 T1-weighted scans from 198 subjects, with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 221.5 Td (gestational age at birth ranging from 26.7 to 44.3 weeks. All scans were acquired at UCSF Benioff Children's) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 206.3 Td (Hospital, San Francisco. Each scan was visually assessed for motion artifacts; 196 scans were labeled as clean) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 191.1 Td (and 128 as motion corrupted. Clean scans were used for model training, and motion-corrupted scans served as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 175.9 Td (the testing set.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 153.6 Td (All images underwent intensity normalization to standardize voxel-wise signal distributions. The model) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 138.4 Td (operated on full 3D volumes rather than 2D slices to better capture spatially coherent motion patterns) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 123.2 Td (distributed across slices in neonatal anatomy.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 101.0 Td (We adopted the MADM, a latent generative framework previously validated in adult MRI motion correction.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 85.7 Td (The architecture includes a Vector Quantized Generative Adversarial Network \(VQGAN\) for encoding and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 70.5 Td (decoding, and a 3D latent diffusion model with an attention-enhanced U-Net for denoising. During training,) Tj ET
endstream
