stream
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 704.8 Td (Gaussian noise was progressively added to the latent representations of clean images in the forward process.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 689.5 Td (The reverse process removed noise conditioned on anatomical priors, reconstructing artifact-free images.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 667.3 Td (To evaluate the model's performance in the absence of ground truth \(i.e., paired images with/without motion\),) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 652.1 Td (we used NIQE \(naturalness image quality evaluator\) to assess perceptual quality and PSNR \(peak) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 636.9 Td (signal-to-noise ratio\) between input and output volumes to quantify denoising performance. All metrics were) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 621.6 Td (computed in 3D to capture whole-brain image quality. We compared the evaluation metrics between MADM) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 606.4 Td (and a previously developed CNN model.) Tj ET
BT /F2 11 Tf 72 577.5 Td (Results, Conclusions, and Discussions) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 559.2 Td (Our model demonstrated consistent improvements in image quality across two evaluation metrics. Compared) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 544.0 Td (to the original motion-corrupted inputs, the corrected images exhibited lower NIQE scores \(reduced from) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 528.8 Td (6.097 to 4.831 by 1.266 on average\), indicating improved perceptual quality. PSNR increased by 2.806 dB,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 513.6 Td (reflecting the model's ability to restore image intensity structure relative to the noisy input. These) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 498.3 Td (improvements were observed consistently across a range of motion severity and gestational age. We further) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 483.1 Td (compared our MADM with a baseline 3D convolutional neural network trained with simulated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 467.9 Td (motion-corrupted images as input, corresponding images as ground truth. MADM consistently outperformed) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 452.7 Td (the CNN across all metrics. Specifically, MADM achieved lower NIQE \(4.831 vs. 5.263\) and higher PSNR) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 437.4 Td (\(26.934 vs. 25.725 dB\). Qualitatively, CNNs were less successful in recovering anatomical details in their) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 422.2 Td (output images and left residual artifacts in regions affected by severe motion. In contrast, MADM preserved) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 407.0 Td (finer details and sharper anatomical boundaries, particularly in key neurodevelopmental features such as the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 391.8 Td (cortical plate, subplate, and early sulcal structures. These enhancements were visually evident in both mild and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 376.5 Td (moderate motion cases, supporting the model's robustness to varying artifact severity.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 354.3 Td (The results demonstrate the capacity of our latent diffusion-based framework to perform effective motion) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 339.1 Td (artifact correction in neonatal brain MRI, even without access to paired clean references. By operating in a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 323.9 Td (learned latent space conditioned on anatomical priors, the model preserves fine structural details while) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 308.6 Td (suppressing motion-induced degradation. The use of full 3D volumes further enables spatially coherent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 293.4 Td (restoration, where motion artifacts often span multiple slices.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 271.2 Td (Clinically, this approach has the potential to avoid repetition of scans, improve diagnostic confidence, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 256.0 Td (enable more reliable downstream analysis to assess early brain development. Future work will focus on) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 240.7 Td (expanding the training dataset to include more varied motion patterns, incorporating simulated motion into the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 225.5 Td (forward process, and evaluating model performance in the segmentation of neuroanatomy and the prediction of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 210.3 Td (clinical outcomes. Overall, our findings support the use of diffusion-based generative models as a practical and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 72 195.1 Td (robust solution to head-motion correction on neonatal brain MRI.) Tj ET
